  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $ABC$ be a right angled triangle with $AB>BC>CA$. Construct three equilateral triangles $BCP$, $CQA$ and $ARB$, so that $A$ and $P$ are on opposite sides of $BC$; $B$ and $Q$ are on opposite sides of $CA$; and $C$ and $R$ are on opposite sides of $AB$. Then",
  "options": {
    "A": "$CR>AP>BQ$",
    "B": "$CR<AP<BQ$",
    "C": "$CR=AP=BQ$",
    "D": "$CR^2=AP^2+BQ^2$"
  },
  "answer": "C",
